            "article_id": "fa41183d662a37f3",
            "title": "Valorant Mobile's MVP Animations: Will They Ever Hit PC? - India Today Gaming",
            "published_at": "Wed, 30 Apr 2025 07:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "India Today Gaming",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://www.indiatodaygaming.com/news/story/valorant-mobiles-mvp-animations-will-they-ever-hit-pc-8410",
            "query_players": [
                "BuZz"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "BuZz"
            ],
            "content": "Valorant Mobile's MVP Animations: Will They Ever Hit PC?\nValorant Mobile’s stylish MVP animations have fans buzzing, but PC players are left in the dust. Will Riot bring these end-of-match showcases to desktop? Here’s what we know and what players are saying.\nValorant Mobile has been making waves with its flashy MVP animations, leaving PC players wondering: Will we ever get these cool end-of-match showcases? Let's dive into what's happening and what the community is saying.\nWhat's the Buzz About?\nValorant Mobile, currently in beta testing, has introduced unique MVP animations for agents. These animations play at the end of a match, highlighting the top player's performance with stylish visuals. For instance:\n- \n Sova draws his bow with flair. \n- \n Phoenix adjusts his jacket confidently. \n- \n Viper activates her abilities with a dramatic pose. \nThese animations have been well-received, with players praising their quality and the added flair they bring to the game.\nPC Players Feeling Left Out\nThe PC community has noticed the absence of these MVP animations in their version of the game. Discussions on Reddit highlight this sentiment:\n\"I feel like the addition of MVP animations to mobile instead of PC... I can’t understand why this isn’t a thing they also added to PC.\"\n— u/ShiraiWasTaken\nSome speculate that different development teams handle mobile and PC features, leading to discrepancies in updates and additions.\nIs There Hope for PC?\nWhile there's no official word from Riot Games about bringing MVP animations to PC, the community remains hopeful. The transition to Unreal Engine 5 might pave the way for such features in the future. As one Reddit user noted:\n\"Can the MVP animation be ported to PC? I don't see why not. Give it some time.\"\n— u/ShiraiWasTaken\nCommunity Reactions\nThe community's reactions are a mix of admiration and frustration:\n- \n Admiration: Players appreciate the quality of the animations and the recognition they provide to top performers. \n- \n Frustration: There's a feeling that PC players are missing out on features that enhance the gaming experience. \nSome players have even expressed envy towards the mobile version, noting that it seems to receive more attention in certain aspects.\nFinal Thoughts\nSo, Valorant Mobile's MVP animations add a fresh layer of excitement, PC players are left wondering when—or if—they'll see similar features. The community's feedback is clear: there's a desire for parity between platforms. Only time will tell if Riot Games will bridge this gap.",
            "content_length": 2531
        },
