                "TenTen",
                "TenZ",
                "YOU"
            ],
            "content": "T1 Entertainment and Sports (T1) has officially announced the highly anticipated matchups for the 2025 LCK Roadshow T1 Home Ground.\nHeld from July 25 to 27, 2025 at Incheon Inspire Arena, attendees can expect an exclusive festival atmosphere featuring live music, interactive fan activities, and vibrant celebrations designed to elevate the thrill of the games.\nThis year, Spotify joins as the event’s main sponsor. This collaboration marks a significant step forward in integrated esports entertainment.\nT1 Home Ground matchups and performances announced\nThe roadshow will host official matches from both LCK (League of Legends Champions Korea) and Valorant (VCT Pacific).\nOpening day on July 25 kicks off with a highly anticipated clash between T1 and Gen.G, alongside other LCK matchups.\nOn July 26, a unique Sibling Derby will take center stage, pitting T1’s Valorant pro, Kim “Meteor” Tae-Oh, against Zeta Division’s Kim “TenTen” Tae-Young. The event also features numerous influencer appearances.\nA pre-show VCT Pacific match will showcase prominent Valorant influencers, including international stars like Tyson “TenZ” Ngo and four other global personalities, alongside Korean participants such as Kim Sung-tae, Bunny Bunny, Do-hyun, Neultur Chunsanghyeob, and Im A-ni.\nThe final day culminates in the intense Red Derby, with T1’s LCK team facing off against Nongshim RedForce and the T1 Esports Academy team playing against DRX Challengers.\nWhat’s more, audiences will be treated to performances by singer and musical theater star Kim Junsu, the popular girl group TripleS, and acclaimed beatboxer WING from BEATPELLA HOUSE. During the halftime show, TransFiction, the band that collaborated with T1 on a custom anthem, will also take the stage.\nFan interaction is expected to reach new heights with enhanced cheering sticks, dedicated fan participation booths, influencer show matches, and more. New cheering traditions, such as team chants, will also be introduced to create a fresh and vibrant atmosphere.\nFor fans eager to experience the full event, the T1 Home Ground 3-Day Pass will be available for purchase. Tickets go on sale at NOL Ticket starting at 2 p.m. KST on June 30, 2025. Additional details regarding ticket prices, the complete schedule, and on-site arrangements will be released via official T1 channels and ticketing platforms.\nREAD MORE: Playtest insights: Yunara is a super traditional marksman who may be too hot for you to handle",
