                "Meteor",
                "TenTen",
                "TenZ"
            ],
            "content": "Global esports organization T1 Entertainment & Sports (T1) has revealed the full lineup for its 2025 LCK Roadshow T1 Home Ground event and announced Spotify as the title sponsor, marking a significant collaboration in competitive gaming and live entertainment.\nThe three-day festival runs July 25–27 at Incheon Inspire Arena and will fuse high-stakes matches with a music and fan-experience showcase. In addition to League of Legends Champions Korea (LCK) and VALORANT Champions Tour (VCT PACIFIC) fixtures, attendees can enjoy live performances, interactive booths and new supporter features designed to boost crowd energy.\nOpening day highlights include T1’s LCK squad taking on Gen.G, plus other league matchups that revisit the intensity of last year’s Mid-Season Invitational. Day two spotlights a rare “Sibling Derby” in VALORANT, pitting T1’s ‘Meteor’ Kim Tae-Oh against ZETA DIVISION’s ‘TenTen’ Kim Tae-Young, and features an influencer pre-show match with North American star ‘TenZ’ Tyson Ngo alongside four international content creators. Homegrown Korean personalities such as Kim Sung-tae, Bunny Bunny, Do-hyun, Neultur Chunsanghyeob and Im A-ni will also compete in the showcase.\nThe finale on July 27 will see T1’s LCK roster face Nongshim RedForce before the T1 Esports Academy team challenges DRX Challengers, rounding out the competitive slate. Throughout the weekend, fans can utilize upgraded cheering sticks, participate in chant workshops and engage with players during meet-and-greets.\nMusical acts will further enliven the occasion, with singer and musical theater performer Kim Junsu, girl group TripleS and beatboxer WING of BEATPELLA HOUSE delivering sets. During halftime, band TransFiction—collaborators on a custom T1 anthem—will energize the crowd with their live performance.\nTickets for the three-day pass go on sale at NOL Ticket starting at 2 p.m. June 30. Detailed pricing, session times and venue logistics will be released on T1’s official channels in the coming weeks. T1 Chief Operating Officer Josh Ahn noted that the partnership with Spotify elevates the Home Ground festival into a fully integrated esports and entertainment experience, inviting fans to shape the event’s atmosphere alongside world-class competition.\n- \n \n I write. I rap. I run. That’s pretty much it. \nSort by:\nComments :0",
