            "content": "Riot Play Club launches new venues in the UK!\nThere are now even more opportunities to come and enjoy VALORANT at Riot Play Club, with new venues joining in April and May! Locations have been added across the UK, and the series of local in-person game nights now spans over a dozen venues across the UK, Finland and Norway.\nThis month sees the launch of Riot Play Club at the Red Bull Gaming Sphere and Platform gaming bar in London, as well as the first ever events in Wales, at Cardiff University, and Northern Ireland returning with Reboot Gaming Cafe! Student events are also being held for the first time at the Universities of Oxford, Northampton, and Roehampton.\nWhether you’re excited for the next VALORANT agent or just want to meet local players, Riot Play Club has something for everyone. Read to the end to find out more about Riot Play Club and discover the location nearest to you!\nWhat is Riot Play Club?\nRiot Play Club is a regular in-person meetup for Riot Games fans to connect, compete, and have fun at local venues around your favourite game. Expect 1v1 challenges, themed quizzes, scavenger hunts as well as custom matches of Swiftplay and Deathmatch with the chance to win exclusive swag.\nEach event is open to all skill levels so bring your squad, or meet new players, and share your best plays with fellow fans in your area. Every club is a bit different depending on the venue and we’ll have new swag drops throughout the year so there’s always something to play for.\nIf you’re more into the esports side of the game then keep an eye on venue socials as we’ll be hosting watch parties throughout the year for VCT EMEA, Masters and also Champions in Paris!\nHow do I join Riot Play Club?\nIt’s easy! Just check the info below to find your nearest event. Venue staff will guide you through the day's activities.\nSome locations may ask you to register for a ticket in advance so make sure you check each venue's social media for details, including any possible entry fees.\nWhen and where is my next Riot Play Club?\nAll venues are listed below, and we regularly update our X and Instagram with new dates. Follow us—and your local clubs—so you never miss a Play Club night!\nSo when and where are the next Riot Play Clubs near me?\nUnited Kingdom\nLondon\n- Razer Store London - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Saturday 12th April \n- GiantX London - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Wednesday 30th April \n- Platform Shoreditch - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: TBA \n- Red Bull Gaming Sphere - Follow them on Instagram for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Saturday 26th April \n- Roehampton University - Students Only - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Friday 11th April \nManchester\nLeeds\nNottingham\n- Nottingham Trent University - Students Only - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Thursday 1st May \nStoke-on-Trent\n- University of Staffordshire - Students Only - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Saturday 12th and Sunday 13th April \nNorthampton\n- University of Northampton - Students Only - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Friday 25th April \nCardiff\n- Cardiff University - Open to the Public - Register to attend here. Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Thursday 10th April \nOxford\n- University of Oxford - Students Only - Follow them on X for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Saturday 3rd May \nBelfast\n- Reboot Gaming Cafe - Follow them on Instagram for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Late April - TBA \nNorway\nOslo\nFinland\nJyväskylä\n- Exen Esports - Follow them on Instagram for updates \n- Next Riot Play Club: Wednesday 23rd April \nDates subject to change - check the local venues for more information and announcements!\nIf you’re interested in becoming a bigger part of Riot Play Club, talk to your local venue staff. We’re always looking for passionate players to run activities locally. It could be a coaching session on your favourite agent, a quiz based around your favourite esports team or a workshop on how you created your favourite cosplay.\nNew Venues\nWe’re looking to expand our Riot Play Clubs out across Northern Europe and will have more venues to announce in the next few months.\nIf you run a venue that you think would be a suitable host in the future, please fill out our application form!",
