            "content": "NAVI esports club has announced its updated VALORANT roster for the upcoming season. Kyrylo «ANGE1» Karasov has been appointed the team's new head coach, replacing Vincent «Happy» Schopenhauer, to whom we extend our gratitude for his contributions throughout last year.\nAndrei «Shao» Kiprskii, Emirhan «hiro» Kat, and Uğur «Ruxic» Güç all maintain their roster spots. They are joined by two new players: Volkan «sociablEE» Yönal (bronze medal at VCT 2025: EMEA Stage 2 as part of BBL Esports) and Dawid «Filu» Czarnecki (formerly of KOI).\nAlaa «Flyn» Nesrallah has also been signed by NAVI to be the team analyst. Flyn previously worked with the Twisted Minds roster and guided them to victory at the Saudi eLeague 2025: Major 2, 3rd place at the Saudi eLeague 2025: Major 3, and Top 6 of the VCT Ascension EMEA 2025.\nKyrylo «ANGE1» Karasov — NAVI VALORANT head coach:\n«I'm excited to begin my coaching journey with NAVI, and I'll do everything I can to bring the team to a level we'll be proud of. It's especially important to be doing this alongside young, yet very talented players.\nYes, we'll have to build a lot from scratch, constantly learn, and make certain adjustments along the way. But I'm confident that we'll put in all our effort and ultimately build a system that can support the team for years to come.»\nNew NAVI VALORANT roster will debut tonight at the Project Blender 2025: Phase 3 tournament. At 18:30 CET, Born to Win will face Team Liquid Academy in a best of 1 match.\nNAVI VALORANT roster:\nAndrei «Shao» Kiprskii\nEmirhan «hiro» Kat\nUğur «Ruxic» Güç\nVolkan «sociablEE» Yönal\nDawid «Filu» Czarnecki\nKyrylo «ANGE1» Karasov (coach)\nDmytro «chippy» Bychenko (assistant coach)\nAlaa «Flyn» Nesrallah (analyst)\nZuzanna «Shiji_mm» Hejduk-Mostowy (performance coach)\nMykhailo «m1ke» Palamar (manager)",
            "content_length": 1813
