            "article_id": "005049cb0769d7a9",
            "title": "Valorant’s Act III Kicks Off Tomorrow As A Celebration Of The Game’s Biggest Moments Ahead Of 5-Year Anniversary - Wccftech",
            "published_at": "Tue, 29 Apr 2025 07:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "Wccftech",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://wccftech.com/valorants-act-iii-kicks-off-tomorrow-as-a-celebration-of-the-games-biggest-moments-ahead-of-5-year-anniversary/",
            "query_players": [
                "Kicks"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "Kicks"
            ],
            "content": "Valorant is set to celebrate its five-year anniversary on June 2, 2025, which is why a key focus to Act III will be celebrating the game's biggest moments in the last five years.\nAct III and the new battle pass will be live tomorrow, April 30, 2025, featuring a special series of anniversary cards that are meant to highlight Valorant's history, including:\n- 5 Years: Duelists Card\n- 5 Years: Cypher's Revenge Card\n- 5 Years: Can't Slow Me Down Card\nRiot's lead for Valorant, Anna Donlon, spoke about the changes the game has gone through in the last five years and the state of the world when Riot first started to launch Valorant and get players into the game.\nShe also talked about how the Valorant team at Riot is working to fix some of the longstanding issues the game has faced in the last five years, and that more information regarding those fixes will be announced in the coming weeks.\nIt'll be interesting to see if those fixes result in any major changes for the game. Some live service games, like Apex Legends, have been through tumultuous changes in recent years as Respawn has tried to satisfy a player base that was growing increasingly unsatisfied with the state of the game. Those same big swings might not happen here, but the potential is there, as Donlon specifically calls out balancing abilities, which could have a huge impact for a hero shooter.\nAs far as what players can expect to see in the game tomorrow with the new battle pass, the free track will include:\n- Killbanner Flex\n- Solarex Sheriff\n- Peeking Vents Spray\n- 5 Years: Duelists Card\n- Squish Ball Buddy\nWhile the paid track for the battle pass will include:\n- Solarex Relic (Melee)\n- Spellbound Bulldog\n- Tacti-Treat Ghost\n- Solarex Phantom\n- Balikbayan Box Spray (Animated)\n- Night Market Conspiracy Spray\n- Boba Truck Buddy\n- 5 Years: Can't Slow Me Down Card\n- 5 Years: Cypher's Revenge Card\nFollow Wccftech on Google to get more of our news coverage in your feeds.",
            "content_length": 1955
        },
