            "article_id": "0341bc130af5e498",
            "title": "Valorant Season 2025 Act 3: Release Date, Patch Notes, And Map Changes - India Today Gaming",
            "published_at": "Tue, 29 Apr 2025 07:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "India Today Gaming",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://www.indiatodaygaming.com/news/story/valorant-season-2025-act-3-release-date-patch-notes-and-map-changes-8411",
            "query_players": [
                "something"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "Life",
                "something",
                "Suggest",
                "YOU"
            ],
            "content": "Valorant Season 2025 Act 3: Release Date, Patch Notes, And Map Changes\nValorant Season 2025 Act 3 brings fresh updates, map changes, and new cosmetics for players.\nThe moment has finally come, and up next is Valorant Season 2025 Act 3. This update has something for everyone: new map changes and fantastic new cosmetics that excite competitive spirits. After all the new Agents and significant drops in maps throughout the year, Riot Games now plans to shift almost completely to fine-tuning the gaming experience and overall reviving the competitive meta, be it for even a ranked grind or lolling here for the skins; something is in this new Act. This will be everything you need to decide before jumping back into the fray.\nValorant Season 2025 Act 3 Release Date and Launch Times\nOfficially, Valorant Season 2025 Act 3 opens April 30, 2025, at 6:00 AM PT in North America, excluding LATAM and Brazil servers. European and Asian players will gain access on May 1, 2025, starting at 4:00 AM BST for Europe. Players should expect a short maintenance window before the patch goes live. Riot will not be slow in confirming the exact downtime update.\nWhat's New in This Act?\nUnlike the past two Acts, no new Agent is coming this time. Riot already introduced Tejo and Waylay early in the year, meaning this third Act will focus more on refining and balancing the existing cast of characters. Act 3 seems unlikely to see the introduction of yet another new map, either. The most recent, Abyss, was only introduced in June 2024, which makes it the freshest battleground. Always possible is the last-minute surprise, but Riot hasn't hinted at anything great yet.\nExpect a lot of quality-of-life changes, small tweaks, and updates that keep competitive play feeling smooth. One of the big competitions that alter the current landscape of competition is the new map pool:\n- The rotation is out for Fracture.\n- Sunset returns are refitted and well-adjusted for the current competitive landscape.\n- Plan for new strategies and compositions as people adapt to the new pool.\nValorant Season 2025 Act 3 Skins, Bundles and Cosmetics\nOn the cosmetic side, Riot is expected to drop the Prelude to Chaos: Volume 2 skin line. Early leaks suggest sleek, futuristic designs with high-end animations-perfect for players who favor style dark and dramatic style.\nIt's not a new wheel that Riot's reinvention in Valorant Season 2025 Act 3; it's just making sure it's a little smoother and sharper, but every bit as thrilling. From shifts in the meta to visual upgrades, there's a lot on the horizon.",
            "content_length": 2575
        },
        {
            "article_id": "dc9bd3659fa8164f",
            "title": "PatMen bucks odds in VCT Pacific - Philstar.com",
            "published_at": "Tue, 29 Apr 2025 07:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "Philstar.com",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://www.philstar.com/sports/2025/04/29/2439237/patmen-bucks-odds-vct-pacific",
            "query_players": [
                "PatMen"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "PatMen"
            ],
            "content": "PatMen bucks odds in VCT Pacific\nMANILA, Philippines — The last Filipino standing in the Valorant Champions Tour (VCT) Pacific-Stage 1, Patrick \"PatMen\" Mendoza, has certainly etched his name as one of the players to watch out for this year.\nPulling off an explosive debut against Boom Esports last April 6, Mendoza bagged two map Most Valuable Player citations, averaging a 235 ACS, and earning the praises of casters and fans alike. This despite Mendoza being on his first international appearance and the first being outside the Philippines.\n\"Before [each] game. I always feel nervous. But once I step on stage, I don't feel anything. I just feel the adrenaline. I just feel the excitement.\" said Mendoza in a post-match interview.\nDespite a strong showing in their recent matches, Mendoza remains committed to improving his gameplay and fully syncing with his teammates as Paper Rex prepares to begin its playoff campaign in the lower bracket.\n\"The first week, when I was practicing with the boys, I'm really lost. There were protocols and calls that I didn't know. But now, I've caught up and I just do what I can to help the team win,” said Mendoza after Paper Rex's win over Global Esports to advance to the playoffs.\nRecalling his journey as a Valorant player, Mendoza had a dream of becoming a pro but never considered being part of Paper Rex, which considered as one of the top teams in the region.\n\"I didn't expect to become part of Paper Rex. Way back 2020 or 2021, I'm just a hard stuck Diamond at that time and because I don't have any FPS background. Valorant is my first game. So basically I'm just watching them before playing against BREN Esports that time but now I'm playing with them,” he added\nWith Paper Rex hoping for redemption after missing the first Valorant Masters of the year, Mendoza is not brushing aside the weight on his shoulders as the new addition to the team.\n\"There's a lot of pressure on me but my mindset is there's no time to be scared, no time to be shy. I'm playing with one of the best so it means I'm also one of the best,\" said Mendoza.\nPaper Rex will face reigning Valorant Masters champion T1 in the lower brackets of the VCT Pacific Stage 1 Playoffs on May 3, at 6 p.m. (Manila time).\n- Latest\n- Trending",
            "content_length": 2254
        },
        {
            "article_id": "ce509c4e150f1f03",
            "title": "Celebrate Five Years of VALORANT: Season 2025 // Act III Kicks off April 30 - Games Press",
            "published_at": "Tue, 29 Apr 2025 07:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "Games Press",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxPN1FqM2cyWXBnaWxWRnYtTEpDSkpzLThtX3F3cFdJclQ4b3JZUnMzLTB5U1BaX2xSRnVMZkl3OWZjRElvdm9PRXBmZHczQzhqTzBpTjFCTk0zU2l0eng0dzFCb00wTnNKZENMRTBqcXlrdU96QzJaWVl1bjZXSHItRXZZY2pwdEE3Skp2QWw3bWNWQWdvRnh2V3d4OUZQQV8wT0ZBT0JR?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://www.gamespress.com/zh-CN/Celebrate-Five-Years-of-VALORANT-Season-2025-Act-III-Kicks-off-April-3",
            "query_players": [
                "Kicks"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "Kicks"
            ],
            "content": "Season 2025 // Act III goes live tomorrow, bringing a new battlepass that is all about celebrating iconic moments from VALORANT’s history as we head into our five-year anniversary. Players will get to experience some nostalgia going all the way back to 2020 through a special series of anniversary-themed player cards such as the 5 Years: Duelists Card, 5 Years: Cypher's Revenge Card and 5 Years: Can't Slow Me Down Card. Some Gun Buddies and Sprays will also evoke memories, including the animated Balikbayan Box Spray and Boba Truck Buddy. \nGifting is coming to VALORANT this act, bringing the ability to gift friends and other players starting with items in the Featured Store. Players will be able to gift whole bundles or individual items, encouraging more ways to celebrate with friends. Alongside Gifting, Duo’s Day is back with a limited-edition capsule featuring the zany duo of Haz and Matt, where players can Gift the bundle to the Haz or Matt in their lives.\nThis act also brings players a new collection, Divergence, where fantasy and otherworldly elements collide in the form of new skins for the Vandal, Classic, Judge, Operator and Staff melee.\nSeason 2025 // Act III goes live on April 30 with the Divergence collection and Duo’s Day limited edition capsule available to players on May 1.\nABOUT VALORANT\nVALORANT is a competitive 5v5 character-based first-person tactical shooter developed and published by Riot Games for PC, Xbox Series X|S and PlayStation®5. VALORANT is a precise and lethal multiplayer game with high-fidelity gunplay, a diverse arsenal of guns, agents with unique abilities, and competitively tuned maps for unlimited hours of play. In VALORANT, players lock in their agent for the entire duration of the match and then attempt to win a round-based, attackers vs. defenders, best-of-24-rounds fight.\nVALORANT is a free-to-play game and optimized to perform on a wide variety of PC and console platforms, allowing for a global audience to compete. Demonstrated by the game’s best-in-class game server quality, global infrastructure, and proprietary anti-cheat technology, Riot Games is committed to preserving the core tenets of the tactical shooter genre and upholding the competitive integrity of the gameplay experience across all available platforms.",
            "content_length": 2292
        },
