            "content": "Rumors: midi Expected to Join Xi Lai Gaming for Masters Toronto 2025\nZhang “midi” Jiajun is reportedly set to join Xi Lai Gaming (XLG) for the upcoming Masters Toronto 2025, according to a report from esports journalist Tanmay, shared via his X account. The team is currently one player short following the recent departure of Yip \"YoU\" Man-ho.\n🛡️ Roster Situation & Background\nXi Lai Gaming earned their spot at Masters Toronto by winning VCT 2025: China Stage 1, but the organization parted ways with YoU shortly after, due to a controversy involving discriminatory comments and other internal issues (previously covered in detail). With the tournament just weeks away, XLG’s active lineup is down to four players, and midi, formerly of Trace Esports, is rumored to be the top candidate to fill the vacancy.\n🌍 Visa Concerns and Timeline\nThe same report notes that Arthur \"Rarga\" Churyumov may be facing visa complications that could affect his travel to Canada. Fortunately, there is still time to resolve the issue ahead of the event.\n📅 Tournament Schedule & Team Outlook\n- Masters Toronto 2025 kicks off on June 7\n- Due to their Stage 1 victory, Xi Lai Gaming will bypass the group stage and begin directly in the playoffs\n- Their first match is scheduled for June 13, giving them a few additional days to complete the roster and address travel issues\nIf confirmed, midi’s addition could bring a much-needed boost to XLG's firepower as they prepare for one of the year's most competitive VALORANT events. Stay tuned for official roster announcements in the days ahead.\n5% deposit bonus up to 100 gems\na free Gift Case\nEGAMERSW - get 11% Deposit Bonus + Bonus Wheel free spin\nEXTRA 10% DEPOSIT BONUS + free 2 spins\n3 Free Cases + 100% up to 100 Coins on First Deposit\n5 Free Cases, Daily FREE & Welcome Bonuses up to 35%\n3 free cases and a 5% bonus added to all cash deposits.\n+5% to deposit",
