            "article_id": "716565c8af254723",
            "title": "Team Vitality Valorant ⇒ 2026 Roster Revealed With Chronicle - Pley.gg",
            "published_at": "Tue, 25 Nov 2025 08:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "Pley.gg",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiekFVX3lxTE5LV0RleURiOGMxSWNtamdMNkFyb292bTRoamdSd1VMa0tlREdyY09BbDRSWkVjSkJmUVhuWTM2REJpSUFBODR6Q2U4eU82c3dSb2Z2M0dFSnc2Q1EtaUNTRHZZZ1NyRXVJNGRmVEt2MmxPVVZON2dheWRn?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://pley.gg/valorant/team-vitality-announces-valorant-roster-2026/",
            "query_players": [
                "Chronicle",
                "Jamppi",
                "PROFEK"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "Chronicle",
                "Derke",
                "Elite",
                "Jamppi",
                "PROFEK"
            ],
            "content": "Team Vitality has officially revealed its new Valorant roster for the 2026 VCT season, entering the year with renewed ambition and one of the most impressive lineups the organization has ever fielded. With the arrival of Chronicle, the promotion of young prodigy Sayonara, and a rebuilt coaching staff, the team is aiming for dominance both in EMEA and on the international stage.\nHere is a full breakdown of the roster, the project behind it, and what fans can expect as Vitality enters a new era.\nVitality rebuilds around elite talent for 2026\nThe club confirmed that Valorant remains a top priority going into 2026. After a strong start to 2025 that included winning the VCT EMEA Kickoff and a Top 4 finish at Masters Bangkok, Vitality fell short of its goals later in the year. The organization responded by assembling a roster built on stability, experience, and long term development.\nTwo major additions headline the project: Timofey “Chronicle” Khromov, one of the best players in the world, and Ștefan “Sayonara” Mîtcu, the youngest rising star in the European scene.\nSayonara will join the active lineup after his 18th birthday and is set to make his VCT EMEA debut in March 2026.\nThe full Team Vitality Valorant roster\nVitality enters 2026 with the following lineup and staff:\nTimofey “Chronicle” Khromov\nElias “Jamppi” Olkkonen\nDawid “PROFEK” Święć\nȘtefan “Sayonara” Mîtcu\nNikita “Derke” Sirmitev\nGregor “PAL” Morton – Head Coach\nBenjamin “Scuttt” Hutchinson – Strategic Coach\nThey will first compete in Project Blender Phase 3 from December 3 to 7, marking the debut of the new structure.\nA roster built to compete for trophies\nCentered around superstar duelist Derke, Team Vitality’s new lineup is designed to be one of the strongest in EMEA.\nChronicle\nOne of the most accomplished players in Valorant, Chronicle brings championship experience, elite consistency, and unrivaled late game composure. After finishing second at three consecutive international events in 2025, he joins Vitality with one goal in mind: winning titles.\nJamppi\nComing off a standout year with BBL Esports, Jamppi steps into the role of in game leader for 2026. His leadership, mechanical level, and synergy with former teammate PROFEK make him a critical part of the team’s structure.\nPROFEK\nA breakout rookie in 2025, PROFEK reunites with Jamppi and coach PAL to bring calm, calculated Controller play to Vitality. His impact performances at BBL Esports solidified his status as one of the most promising Controller players in EMEA.\nSayonara\nAt only 17, Sayonara has already made history by becoming the youngest winner and MVP in the Spanish Challengers League. His explosive performances and rapid rise through the French and Spanish scenes make him one of the top young prospects globally.\nDerke\nRegarded as one of the greatest duelists in Valorant history, Derke enters 2026 as the team’s centerpiece. His legendary 2023 season, paired with strong results for Vitality in 2025, places high expectations on his role as the team’s star fragger.\nCoaching staff leading the new project\nVitality’s rebuilt coaching team features two highly respected names.\nPAL – Head Coach\nPAL arrives after an impressive year with BBL Esports, where he led the team to a Top 3 finish in VCT EMEA Stage 2. He brings a strong strategic vision and reunites with both Jamppi and PROFEK.\nScuttt – Strategic Coach\nWith experience from Fnatic and multiple international finals in 2025, Scuttt provides deep analytical expertise. His partnership with PAL strengthens the team’s long term planning and in game preparation.\nA familiar face is expected to temporarily support the team at the start of the season until Sayonara officially joins in March.\nVitality’s vision for 2026\nTeam Vitality enters the new season with the ambition to establish itself as a perennial contender at the top of the global Valorant scene. The roster is built around shared values of trust, discipline, and cohesion, aiming to create a culture that prioritizes long term success.\nSupporting the development of Sayonara and leaning on the leadership of Chronicle, Derke, and Jamppi, the club hopes to build a strong foundation capable of competing for VCT titles and eventually the Valorant Champions trophy.\nThe team will debut together at Project Blender 2025 on December 3, kicking off a new chapter for Vitality with fresh momentum and high expectations.\nFor more Valorant news, roster moves, and esports coverage, check out Pley.gg.\nSource: SwipeRight.gg",
            "content_length": 4503
        },
