            ],
            "content": "The NRG Esports esports organization has officially certified the signing of a long-term agreement with its professional Valorant player Ethan “Ethan” Arnold. Contractual obligations for the long-term process are calculated until the end of 2027, securing the status of a key team member for the two-time world champion. The NRG organization shared the news of the esports scene through official platforms.\nTable of Contents\nThe updated playing line-up includes:\n- \n \n \n \n Ethan “Ethan” Arnold\n- \n \n \n \n Adam “mada” Pampukh\n- \n \n \n \n Brock “brawk” Somerhalder\n- \n \n \n \n Logan “skuba” Jenkins\nEthan’s professional career in the tactical shooter from Riot Games shows steady progress on the career ladder. The NRG player has proven himself through his playing skills and team dynamics in international competitions.\nThe launch season of OW Contenders 2018 is scheduled for March. Seven participants received direct invitations to the Overwatch tournament. Among other things, three winners of the first season of 2017 and two leading Trials teams will take part in the Contenders competitions.\nTeam training sessions and training schedules are aimed at participating in esports tournaments. The game discipline of the roaster strategy is focused on achieving tournament prizes and strengthening the ranking among professional teams.\nBy the way, before signing Ethan, NRG announced that they had parted ways with their professional player Sam s0m. He left NRG after five years of playing for them, and he was an important member of the VALORANT team.\nPlayer transitions and contract negotiations show how esports is changing. The new deal with Ethan shows that the management wants to assemble a strong team to perform well at the championships.\nThe details of the contract and how much money will be paid are not being disclosed. Right now, NRG is focused on preparing for important tournaments and making sure the players get along well with each other.",
