            ],
            "content": "Valorant Pride Month 2025 Drops: Title and Buddy Revealed\nValorant’s Pride month 2025 rewards are going to be here in June. Find out how to unlock this year’s special drops, what makes them unique, and why they’re creating buzz in the community.\nValorant’s Pride 2025 rewards are here with fresh ways to rep your pride in-game. Find out how to unlock this year’s special drops, what makes them unique, and why they’re creating buzz in the community.\nValorant’s Pride 2025 rewards just leaked — and this year, it’s all about living as yourself, no matter who you love. These drops? All vibes. And a little flex. Okay, maybe a lot. Let’s get into it.\nWhat’s in Valorant’s Pride 2025 Drop?\nREMINDER // Pride 2025 Rewards // #VALORANT\n— VALORANT Leaks & News (@VALORANTLeaksEN) May 26, 2025\n• ''Flyby Hug'' Gunbuddy\n• ''Ate'' Title pic.twitter.com/MennPAWnrM\n- \n “Ate” Title – You already told the lobby how it’s gonna go. One-taps incoming? Of course. You ate. \n- \n “Flyby Hug” Gun Buddy – A tiny burst of love for your weapon. Unexpected? Maybe. Adorable? Absolutely. \nThese cosmetics are fun, free, and made to let you wear your pride in style — whether that’s pride in identity, gameplay, or both. The “Ate” title alone is the kind of thing that’ll get you pre-muted in lobbies (and still leave top fragging — unless you’re bottom fragging... awkward).\nHow to Get the “Ate” Title and Flyby Hug Buddy in Valorant\nHere’s the best part: there are no codes, no store tab, and no missions involved. Just log in to Valorant between June 1 and June 27, 2025, and the Pride 2025 rewards will automatically be added to your account. That’s it, no catch involved! It's for free\nThese items are part of Riot’s ongoing LGBTQ+ support, giving players more ways to express themselves freely — in-game and beyond.\nAlso Read: Valorant Masters Toronto Drops: Here’s What You Get for Just Watching\nFinal Thoughts\nWhether you’re stacking with your usual five or solo queueing, these Pride drops let you be you. Equip the “Ate” title, throw on the Flyby Hug, and let the scoreboard do the talking. Pride season in Valorant? It’s not quiet. It’s bold, fun, and a celebration of every kind of player — exactly how it should be. The most important part? Riot isn’t monetizing pride month by taking advantage of how someone is, especially when they’re making beta players buy the beta bundle as well. What do you think? W or L move by riot?\nWritten By: Sarah Dar (Writing Intern, India Today Gaming)",
