            "content": "The Game Awards is currently ongoing as I write this, and now it’s time to crown some winners in between world premiere trailers for upcoming games. And then ad breaks that are also trailers for upcoming games.\nThe awards themselves can be controversial, but everyone does want to see what takes home the top prizes every year, as if there is a place that crowns a definitive GOTY. It’s The Game Awards; like it or not, there will no doubt be a host of snubs that everyone will be talking about tomorrow, but there are always loads of deserving winners as well.\nThe main question heading into the show is if Sandfall’s Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 can be upset by any other game, given its record number of nominations and clear path to GOTY. It seems unlikely, but we’ll see how the night progresses. It would not be the first supposed sure-thing to be unseated by a dark horse, after all.\nThe full list of the nominees is below, which I will update as these awards are doled out. Some are in the pre-show, others are listed rapid fire as they are every year in a program that probably has too many categories at baseline. So, here we go, and you can refresh for updates:\nGame of the Year\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - It may have been a bit of an anticlimax, but it’s a deserved win for what is truly a generational game and one that has become one of my favorite I’ve ever played. I cannot recommend it enough.\n- Death Stranding 2: On the Beach\n- Donkey Kong Bananza\n- Hades II\n- Hollow Knight: Silksong\n- Kingdom Come: Deliverance II\nBest Game Direction\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - I’m writing this as it was just announced as the second-to-last award of the show, and I think we all know what’s coming next.\n- Death Stranding 2: On The Beach\n- Ghost of Yōtei\n- Hades II\n- Split Fiction\nBest Adaptation\n- A Minecraft Movie\n- Devil May Cry\n- The Last of Us: Season 2 (WINNER) - This would be a bit of a surprise, given that season 2 was not widely liked in many regards compared to the first, but its competition this year was…less than steep.\n- Splinter Cell: Deathwatch\n- Until Dawn\nBest Narrative\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - Of all its strengths, and it has many, the game is here mainly because of the power of its narrative which many would argue makes it a stellar game.\n- Death Stranding 2: On The Beach\n- Ghost of Yōtei\n- Kingdom Come: Deliverance II\n- Silent Hill f\nBest Art Direction\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - One of the most beautiful games I’ve ever seen literally based around the world being a painting, so yes, well-deserved.\n- Death Stranding 2: On The Beach\n- Ghost of Yōtei\n- Hades II\n- Hollow Knight: Silksong\nBest Score And Music\n- Hollow Knight: Silksong\n- Hades II\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - I’ve been listening to this OST for months, and it deserves the win.\n- Ghost of Yōtei\n- Death Stranding 2: On the Beach\nBest Audio Design\n- Battlefield 6 (WINNER) - First outright loss for Expedition 33, but if you’ve played Battlefield, you probably get it.\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33\n- Death Stranding 2: On the Beach\n- Ghost of Yōtei\n- Silent Hill f\nBest Performance\n- Ben Starr (Expedition 33)\n- Charlie Cox (Expedition 33)\n- Erika Ishii (Ghost of Yotei)\n- Jennifer English (Expedition 33) - She played central heroine Maelle in the game and was, of course, excellent – tying the entire narrative together. I would have been all for Ben Starr, however, or the not-nominated Andy Serkis from the game.\n- Konatsu Kato (Silent Hill f)\n- Troy Baker (Indiana Jones and the Great Circle)\nInnovation In Accessibility\n- Assassin’s Creed Shadows\n- Atomfall\n- Doom: The Dark Ages (WINNER)\n- EA Sports FC 26\n- South of Midnight\nGames for Impact\n- Consume Me\n- Despelote\n- Lost Records: Bloom & Rage\n- South of Midnight (WINNER)\n- Wanderstop\nBest Ongoing Game\n- Final Fantasy XIV\n- Fortnite\n- Helldivers 2\n- Marvel Rivals\n- No Man’s Sky (WINNER) - Once a cautionary tale for overpromising and under delivering, No Man’s Sky has now pumped out so many free updates it is practically an entirely different game many times over.\nBest Community Support\n- Baldur’s Gate 3 (WINNER)\n- Final Fantasy XIV\n- Fortnite\n- Helldivers 2\n- No Man's Sky\nBest Independent Game\n- Absolum\n- Ball x Pit\n- Blue Prince\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - The first win for Expedition 33 for the evening, first of many, most likely. This category does have three of the six GOTY nominees in it, interestingly. Beating those two means it’s effectively impossible for either Hades or Silksong to win GOTY over Expedition 33 later in the night.\n- Hades II\n- Hollow Knight: Silksong\nBest Debut Indie Game\n- Blue Prince\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - If it won Best Indie, it was essentially impossible to lose this, and here we are.\n- Despelote\n- Dispatch\nBest Mobile Game\n- Destiny: Rising\n- Persona 5: The Phantom X\n- Sonic Rumble\n- Umamusume: Pretty Derby (WINNER)\n- Wuthering Waves\nBest VR/AR Game\n- Alien: Rogue Incursion\n- Arken Age\n- Ghost Town\n- Marvel’s Deadpool VR\n- The Midnight Walk (WINNER)\nBest Action Game\n- Battlefield 6\n- Doom: The Dark Ages\n- Hades II (WINNER) - Certainly the most deserving on the list, but as the only GOTY nominee, it was a sure thing here.\n- Ninja Gaiden 4\n- Shinobi: Art of Vengeance\nBest Action Adventure Game\n- Death Stranding 2: On the Beach\n- Ghost of Yōtei\n- Indiana Jones and the Great Circle\n- Hollow Knight: Silksong (WINNER) - Since it beat fellow GOTY contender Death Stranding 2, that’s now out for that award. But so is Silksong after it lost best Indie to E33.\n- Split Fiction\nBest RPG\n- Avowed\n- Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (WINNER) - Expedition 33 beats KCDII, so it’s just heading up against Donkey Kong for the final.\n- Kingdom Come: Deliverance II\n- The Outer Worlds 2\n- Monster Hunter Wilds\nBest Fighting Game\n- 2XKO\n- Capcom Fighting Collection 2\n- Fatal Fury: City of the Wolves (WINNER)\n- Mortal Kombat: Legacy Kollection\n- Virtua Fighter 5 R.E.V.O. World Stage\nBest Family Game\n- Donkey Kong Bananza (WINNER)\n- LEGO Party!\n- LEGO Voyagers\n- Mario Kart World\n- Sonic Racing: CrossWorlds\n- Split Fiction\nBest Sim/Strategy Game\n- The Alters\n- FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles\n- Jurassic World Evolution 3\n- Sid Meier's Civilization VII\n- Tempest Rising\n- Two Point Museum\nBest Sports/Racing\n- EA Sports FC 26\n- F1 25\n- Mario Kart World (WINNER)\n- Rematch\n- Sonic Racing: CrossWorlds\nBest Multiplayer\n- Arc Raiders (WINNER) - One of the biggest success stories of the year right alongside Expedition 33, this is something no one else would have called even months ago.\n- Battlefield 6\n- Elden Ring Nightreign\n- Peak\n- Split Fiction\nMost Anticipated Game\n- 007 First Light\n- Grand Theft Auto VI (WINNER)\n- Marvel's Wolverine\n- Resident Evil Requiem\n- The Witcher IV\nContent Creator of the Year\n- Caedrel\n- Kai Cenat\n- MoistCr1TiKaL (WINNER)\n- Sakura Miko\n- The Burnt Peanut\nBest Esports Game\n- Counter-Strike 2 (WINNER)\n- Dota 2\n- League of Legends\n- Mobile Legends: Bang Bang\n- Valorant\nBest Esports Athlete\n- brawk\n- Chovy (WINNER)\n- f0rsakeN\n- Kakeru\n- MenaRD\n- Zyw0o\nBest Esports Team\n- Gen.G - League of Legends\n- NRG - Valorant\n- Team Falcons - DOTA 2\n- Team Liquid PH - Mobile Legends: Bang Bang\n- Team Vitality - Counter-Strike 2 (WINNER)\nPlayers’ Voice\n- Expedition 33\n- Dispatch\n- Genshin Impact\n- Hollow Knight: Silksong\n- Wuthering Waves (WINNER) - Hey, Expedition 33 lost something\nFollow me on Twitter, YouTube, Bluesky and Instagram.",
            "content_length": 7484
        },
