            "article_id": "1d7be95207e7969d",
            "title": "Valorant x Fragment x Nike Air Force 1: an exclusive collaboration between gaming, fashion and sneakers - selecta bisso",
            "published_at": "Mon, 06 Oct 2025 07:00:00 GMT",
            "source": "selecta bisso",
            "google_news_url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
            "article_url": "https://selectabisso.com/en/Valorant-x-Fragment-x-Nike-Air-Force-1%3A-an-exclusive-collaboration-between-gaming--fashion--and-sneakers/",
            "query_players": [
                "BuZz"
            ],
            "matched_players": [
                "BuZz",
                "NaturE"
            ],
            "content": "A new phenomenon has just emerged at the intersection of video games, urban culture, and luxury streetwear. Presented exclusively at the \"VLRNTFRGMT\" pop-up in Paris, the Nike Air Force 1 Low in collaboration with Valorant et Fragment Design is already creating a buzz. This unique triple crossover could well become one of the most coveted sneaker releases of 2025.\nA rare fusion of three powerful universes\nThis collaboration marks a first: the video game giant Riot Games, via its successful FPS Valorant, associates with Fragment Design, the label founded by the cult designer Hiroshi fujiwara, and to Nike, one of the pillars of sneaker culture. A trio that may seem surprising, but ultimately, not so much.\nValorant embodies the cyberfuturistic and competitive world of e-sports, adored by millions of players around the world.\nFragment Design, known for his ultra-sleek minimalism and conceptual approach to design, has already left an indelible mark on fashion and the rarest sneaker collaborations.\nNike, finally, brings its heritage and its legendary Air Force 1, an essential silhouette since 1982.\nThis blend results in a sneaker that straddles the line between virtual world and physical reality, with almost architectural precision.\nA minimalist and conceptual design by Fujiwara\nLa Nike Air Force 1 Low Valorant x Fragment boasts a sleek, stealthy aesthetic that's true to Fujiwara's signature approach. Crafted entirely from premium black leather, it features tonal stitching and subtle embossed details on the midsole: \"VLNT\" and \"FRGMT.\"\nCo-branding elements are subtle yet powerful: Fragment's lightning bolt logo and Valorant's iconic \"V\" are stamped on the heels, adding a touch of mystery to this ultra-clean black sneaker.\nThis collaboration embodies a cultural evolution: the fusion of the virtual world of video games, Japanese conceptual design, and American streetwear heritage. The Nike Air Force 1 Valorant x Fragment Design is a hybrid collectible, at the intersection of digital and real, style and gameplay.\nAn exclusive release… for now\nThis limited edition was distributed only during the Parisian pop-up, accompanied by collector packaging: each pair comes with two plush toys inspired by the Valorant universe and a co-branded carrying bag, reinforcing the premium and collectible nature of the release. No global distribution plans have yet been announced by Nike, which is already fueling speculation and excitement among sneakerheads and gaming fans. One thing is certain: this triple collaboration could remain one of the rarest Holy Grails of the year!",
